{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>Until the Jubilee year.</b> For his entire self was acquired only to work him until the Jubilee, for in the Jubilee he goes free, as is stated below: ״וְיָצָא בִּשְׁנַת הַיֹּבֵל״; and Scripture speaks of a gentile under your hand (Sifra; Kiddushin 16), and even so you may not come upon him with trickery because of the desecration of the Name (Bava Kamma 113) — rather, when he comes to redeem himself, he calculates precisely: according to what accrues each and every year, the gentile deducts from his money. If there were twenty years from when he was sold until the Jubilee, and he acquired him for twenty maneh, it turns out the gentile acquired a year's labor for one maneh; and if this one stayed with him five years and comes to redeem himself, he deducts five maneh from him, and the slave gives him fifteen maneh. And this is <b>And the money of his sale shall be by the number of years</b>." "<b>Like the days of a hireling shall he be with him</b> — he calculates what accrues to each and every year, as though he hired himself to him each year for one maneh, and he deducts from him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:32.287357710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}